      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-106368",
      ":question/problem": "A laboratory test for a particular disease is conducted on some patients. Of the tested patients, $95%$ of those infected and $2%$ of those not infected tested positive for the disease. Only $20%$ of the entire population is infected with the disease. What is the probability that a randomly chosen patient that tested negative is infected? Round your answer to four decimal places.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
